# Claude Code — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md` and **not** `AGENTS.md`, so this file imports the
contract rather than restating it: an `@path` import is expanded into context at
session start, so the imported file arrives in full. One file states the
contract and every runtime loads it — a per-runtime copy is a fork, and a fork
drifts.

Anything below this line is Claude-only. Anything that must reach every runtime
belongs in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).

- Path-scoped rules in `.claude/rules/` bind **this runtime only**. Put nothing
  there that a session on another runtime also needs.
